# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Game text is copyrighted. Konami's script (English or Japanese), the PS2
# Korean localization, and Shinsnote's transcription of it must never be
# committed -- not as data, not as evidence, not quoted inside documentation.
# Only tools, byte-level format notes, and counts belong in this repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/decisions/
/docs/*-2026-08-16.md
/docs/SESSION-*.md
/docs/ps2*
/docs/**/ps2*
*shinsnote*
*_ps2_*
*ps2_korean*

# Pattern rules, so a new evidence dump cannot slip through by being dated later.
# These artefacts are per-line dumps of the script by construction: they carry the
# `english` and `korean` field of every row they report on.
/docs/evidence/**/partial-application-*
/docs/evidence/**/*-block.csv
/docs/evidence/**/*-dialogue-*.csv
/docs/evidence/**/*-worklist-*.csv
/docs/evidence/**/codec-round*-proposed-*
# Per-row rewrite tables (find/replace pairs): these ARE the script by construction.
/docs/evidence/**/reg_*
/docs/evidence/**/fix_*
# Keep the aggregate reports that carry only counts and addresses:
!/docs/evidence/**/coverage-*.json
!/docs/evidence/**/round5-gate.json

# evidence files that embed game script
